Title: Wythall PE teacher hails ex-student Glasspool for Wimbledon title win
Date: 2025-07-14
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Joe Maidment', 'Text': '"To think a student from Woodrush High School in Wythall can win at Wimbledon - it\'s just amazing."', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 84}}, {'Speaker': 'Joe Maidment', 'Text': '"It should be a message to everyone in the West Midlands to follow their dreams and see what they can achieve," he added.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 3, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 119}}, {'Speaker': 'Joe Maidment', 'Text': '"I can now say I\'ve played tennis against a Wimbledon champion. Unfortunately, I did lose 6-0, 6-0, and he was only in year eight at the time.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 121}}, {'Speaker': 'Joe Maidment', 'Text': '"I am so, so pleased for him and everyone involved," Mr Maidment added.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 7, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 67}}, {'Speaker': 'Joe Maidment', 'Text': 'He described the title as "the icing on the cake" for the 31-year-old and said after he had now won Wimbledon, Queens and Eastbourne, his former student had secured "the triple crown".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 8, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 160}}, {'Speaker': 'Lloyd Glasspool', 'Text': '"I\'ve come a long way since when we played in year seven or eight and I gave you that little thrashing," Glasspool said to him.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 12, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 110}}, {'Speaker': 'Lloyd Glasspool', 'Text': '"It gave me a nice little confidence boost to go and do great things in the sport.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 13, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 76}}, {'Speaker': 'Lloyd Glasspool', 'Text': '"I appreciate the support from you and the whole of the Woodrush School," the men\'s doubles champion added.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 101}}], 'Description': [{'Description': "PE teacher Joe Maidment is in awe of his former student Lloyd Glasspool, who, alongside his partner Julian Cash, made history on Saturday when they became the first all-British pair to win the men's doubles title at the All England Club for 89 years.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 220}}, {'Description': 'Mr Maidment had travelled to Wimbledon to watch Glasspool, 31, from Redditch, in his second-round match in west London and said his performance throughout the tournament had been "inspirational".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 2, 'StartChar': 221, 'EndChar': 359}}, {'Description': "Mr Maidments said Glasspool, who is a member of the Warwickshire Lawn Tennis Association, had sent a video message to the school from the courts at SW19 ahead of the school's recent annual sports awards.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 10, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 168}}, {'Description': "He added that he also received a personal thank-you message from his former student after Saturday's final.", 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 11, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 94}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': "Two male tennis players, Lloyd Glasspool and Julian Cash, after their Wimbledon men's doubles win on Centre Court Wimbledon. They are both wearing white Adidas tennis tops and white caps."}]}
